title: Linux Update Tracker: Pending reboot
agents: linux
catalog: os/misc
license: GPLv2
distribution: https://github.com/KeksDipp/checkmk-plugins
description:
 Shows whether the host needs a reboot after updates, and since when.
 Detected via {/run/reboot-required}, a newer installed kernel than the running
 one, core packages (kernel, glibc, systemd, ...) installed after the last boot
 on RPM systems and {needrestart}. Inside containers the kernel is ignored.
 Default: {WARN} after 1 day, {CRIT} after 3 days. With "No levels" the
 service always stays {OK}.

 Services still running old libraries are listed (needrestart,
 dnf needs-restarting, zypper ps). By default they do not change the state.

discovery:
 One service is created if the agent plugin output is present.
